From e587931bd083dd5813e3f9b852eaa37ebf4da595 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 22:13:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08564/11362] [outer-loop] Phase 0b: gate remaining think-mode
 fences, forward repeat_penalty on chat route

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6198 Phase 0b. Two of three induce-prompt call shapes in
LocalGGUFProposer.generate() still unconditionally pre-opened a code
fence, silently suppressing model reasoning even when think mode was
on -- only the combined-induce call was gated on induce_think_on().
Fixed the split-induce engine-half fallback and _goal_only_prompt() to
match, with new regression tests for both.

_chat_complete_request() dropped repeat_penalty/repeat_last_n entirely.
Since think mode forces the chat-completions route regardless of
use_chat_template, every think-mode engine-induce call was losing
repetition control. Added the params through the signature, payload,
retry call, and the one call site in generate(), with tests confirming
both the forwarding and the not-required-skip case.

Documented (not fixed -- confirmed dormant/unreachable today) a related
use_chat_template+_codeonly truncation bug at the _codeonly computation
site, and corrected four stale "default OFF" comments left over from
the 2026-08-08 think-mode default flip.

Regression sweep across the 35 files reachable from these two modules
found 41 pre-existing failures across 7 files (up from the previously
documented 17/2) -- confirmed identical via git-stash clean-HEAD
comparison, so none are newly introduced; scope addendum filed in
known-issues.md rather than silently absorbing the larger number.

13 results/*.json artifacts carry freshness_acknowledgements entries
for this change (verified-inert against their own measured code paths
via git diff hunk inspection), including one second-order cascade
entry where acknowledging drift in two cited artifacts changed their
hashes and re-staled a third that cites them by content hash.

